Thomas Weyand's submission for Main Quest 1

HOW TO RUN
  In the Unity Editor, press the play button while in the MainMenu scene.
  The game should be set to the 1920x1080 resolution.

  If running from a build, just double click the DragonGuesser.exe file.

CONTROLS
  All you need is a mouse with a left click in order to click the onscreen buttons.

KNOWN ISSUES
  The smoke effect can sometimes obfuscate the Dragon's face on the death screen.
  There is no alert for an invalid input, the keypad just resets to 0.
  If you try to put in a number into the keypad that goes.
  If the game is not played with the "Full HD (1920x1080)" or "16x9 Aspect", then the game does not work properly.
  [FIXED] The GuessingPhase does not start when in "16x9 Aspect"
          - I imagine it has to do with how I coded the keypad moving offscreen, because the guessing display works fine if you manually turn it on.
          -[SOLUTION] 16x9 Aspect caused the y value keypad to change, so I had the keypad mover use only the x coordinate to validate the keypad's movement instead.
  The Keypad moves too fast when played in "16x9" aspect mode.
